 "title": "Choosing the right material",
 "audience": "family",
 "keyIdea": "We choose a material because its properties suit the job.",
 "explain": {
  "kid": [
   "An umbrella must keep rain off, so we need a waterproof material. Paper would get soggy!",
   "Think about what the job needs, then pick a material that does it."
  ],
  "adult": [
   "Ask two questions: what does the job need (waterproof, see-through, stiff, soft)? Which material has that property? Then explain the choice with 'because'.",
   "Some materials fail in funny ways: a chocolate teapot melts, a paper umbrella soaks through. These help children reason about properties."
  ]
 },
